<title>UK: SmithKline shares up on FDA panel news.</title>
<headline>SmithKline shares up on FDA panel news.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in SmithKline Beecham Plc climbed on Friday after a U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA) advisory panel recommended approval of the pharmaceutical group's carvedilol drug for heart failure, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares were 10-1/2p firmer at 934 by 0833 GMT.  </p>
<p>&quot;The news on their heart drug gave them an early boost,&quot; one market-maker said.</p>
<p>The FDA does not have to follow the panel's advice, but usually does.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
